<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n42475" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐρῑν-άζω</span></b> , aor. I inf.
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐρινάξαι</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐρινάσαι,</span>
		<i><span class="en">
			Hsch.
		</span></i>:—<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>hang
				fruiting branches of the wild fig</i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐρινεός</span>) <i>near the cultivated fig</i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">συκῆ</span>) in order that the gall-insect (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ψήν</span>) which lives in the wild fruit may
			carry pollen to the <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σῦκον,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>CP</u>
				2.9.5
			</span></i>:—
				Pass.
			, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ ἐρινασμένον</span>”
				<i>the fig subjected to caprification,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>HP</u>
					2.8.3
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>gather wild figs,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Poll.
				7.143
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
